ne or both eligible MMR doses should be supported to complete vaccination.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"MUMPS_06","direct_score_input":false},{"row":67,"status":"PASS_MUMPS_07","source":"UKHSA mumps prevention and immunisation","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/mumps-the-green-book-chapter","verified":"Public-health professionals should use the current Green Book chapter and its update patches.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"MUMPS_07","direct_score_input":false},{"row":68,"status":"PASS_MUMPS_08","source":"UKHSA mumps prevention and immunisation","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/mmrv-vaccination/mmrv-vaccination-a-guide-for-parents-and-carers","verified":"MMRV protects children against measles, mumps, rubella and varicella.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"MUMPS_08","direct_score_input":false},{"row":69,"status":"PASS_WITH_MUMPS_09","source":"UKHSA mumps prevention and immunisation","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/mumps-the-green-book-chapter","verified":"Mumps risk depends on immunity, contact intensity, setting, age, symptoms and timing of exposure.","quality_score":"3","adoption":"MUMPS_GUARD_09","direct_score_input":false},{"row":70,"status":"PASS_WITH_MUMPS_10","source":"UKHSA mumps prevention and immunisation","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/mumps-the-green-book-chapter","verified":"Mumps evidence is case-, contact-, vaccination-, setting- and time-specific and is not an exact parcel-level infection probability.","quality_score":"3","adoption":"MUMPS_GUARD_10","direct_score_input":false},{"row":71,"status":"PASS_RUBELLA_01","source":"UKHSA rubella and pregnancy protection","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/rubella-the-green-book-chapter","verified":"Rubella is generally a mild illness caused by a togavirus.","quality_score":"4","adoption":"RUBELLA_01","direct_score_input":false},{"row":72,"status":"PASS_RUBELLA_02","source":"UKHSA rubella and pregnancy protection","url":